  "fix_decisions": [
    {
      "finding_id": "F-1",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "c0ac9286df9e6e4b35aa2d910b4eb515178afa68",
      "evidence": "All four anchored regex checks in src/sqllens/rule_sets.py now use fullmatch, so '7\\n' is refused as an invalid user ID (criterion 9: '7a' and other non-digit text refused); permission_fingerprint, application_commit and generated_on validators likewise. Test: test_invalid_user_ids_are_refused gains '7\\n' and ' 7'. Class sweep: config.py _RLS_IDENTIFIER_RE.match sites are pre-existing flat-RLS code (blame 3aff6243), left."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-2",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "c0ac9286df9e6e4b35aa2d910b4eb515178afa68",
      "evidence": "RefusalRedactingRunner skips its WARNING when the refusal's direct cause is not a guard refusal or parse error: that is exactly each guard's fail-closed path, which already logged the cause with a traceback. Criterion 26 (one WARNING record carrying the full reason) now holds for those paths; other refusals still log once. Test: test_guard_logged_unexpected_error_writes_one_warning; existing one-warning parametrized test still passes."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "VC-111",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "c0ac9286df9e6e4b35aa2d910b4eb515178afa68",
      "evidence": "verify-memory now checks for a configured rule-set file right after Config.load, before the --format and API-key checks, so every configured case prints the rule-set message and exits 1 before any case. Test: test_verify_memory_rule_set_message_precedes_other_checks (bad format, missing API key)."
    }
  ],
